1
00:00:00,520 --> 00:00:02,332
Every device says safe.

2
00:00:02,282 --> 00:00:07,015
Extraction is down, hot work is active, and four people enter the gas corridor.

3
00:00:07,015 --> 00:00:10,153
Compound Zero connects the weak signals before disaster.

4
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:17,574
Industrial sites already have sensors, permits, maintenance systems, and worker-location data.

5
00:00:17,524 --> 00:00:19,447
The blind spot is between them.

6
00:00:19,447 --> 00:00:25,559
Compound Zero is a predictive safety layer that turns fragmented evidence into an explainable, human-gated safety case.

7
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:36,721
This is a deterministic, model-backed simulated replay at Coke Battery Four.

8
00:00:36,671 --> 00:00:40,326
Extraction fan E-F zero four is isolated for maintenance.

9
00:00:40,326 --> 00:00:42,533
Gas channels begin rising together.

10
00:00:42,533 --> 00:00:47,903
Then a hot-work permit becomes active nearby, and four contractor badges enter the exposure contour.

11
00:01:05,400 --> 00:01:12,333
Fusion first crosses its intervention threshold at T-plus nine—thirteen minutes before the authored harmful state at T-plus twenty-two.

12
00:01:12,283 --> 00:01:14,378
Every device alarm is clear.

13
00:01:14,378 --> 00:01:21,274
By T-plus eighteen, hot work and four workers expand the evidence; the model score reaches one hundred with four minutes remaining.

14
00:01:21,274 --> 00:01:26,162
Combustible gas is still about eight-point-six percent L-E-L against a twenty-percent threshold.

15
00:01:32,400 --> 00:01:34,678
The alert is not a generated story.

16
00:01:34,628 --> 00:01:41,076
Its evidence graph links the correlated gas trend to the impaired extraction barrier, the ignition-source permit, and exposed people.

17
00:01:41,076 --> 00:01:44,145
Every input carries a timestamp and source receipt.

18
00:01:44,145 --> 00:01:49,076
The risk path is a calibrated gradient-boosting model with structured evidence—not an LLM.

19
00:02:03,400 --> 00:02:07,747
Compound Zero proposes controls and previews a non-causal simulated estimate.

20
00:02:07,697 --> 00:02:13,972
The safety officer selects Hold Hot-Work Permit, sees risk project from one hundred to seventy-one, and records a dry run.

21
00:02:13,972 --> 00:02:15,834
Residual risk stays visible.

22
00:02:15,834 --> 00:02:21,447
No field action is executed, and existing alarms and safety-instrumented systems remain independent.

23
00:02:25,400 --> 00:02:35,997
The same simulated case then passes through four bounded services: anonymous CCTV event metadata, numeric fusion, a locally searched and cited incident-pattern corpus, and deterministic permit-evidence checks.

24
00:02:35,947 --> 00:02:37,972
Missing evidence remains visible.

25
00:02:37,972 --> 00:02:46,016
A response plan can be approved by three simulated roles, but the API records authorization only—actuation stays none and execution stays manual.

26
00:02:48,400 --> 00:02:53,703
On a whole-seed holdout, fusion detects all sixty-five simulated events with twelve-minute median lead.

27
00:02:53,653 --> 00:02:59,007
A harder scenario-type holdout falls to eighty-percent pooled recall and misses unseen process drift.

28
00:02:59,007 --> 00:03:04,895
Missing critical streams also falls to eighty percent; sensor noise preserves recall but multiplies false alarms.

29
00:03:04,895 --> 00:03:08,688
That failure keeps deployment behind site-calibrated shadow validation.

30
00:03:14,400 --> 00:03:20,384
The decision, model version, input receipts and dry-run outcome travel together in one unsigned JSON evidence pack.

31
00:03:20,334 --> 00:03:26,016
Deployment starts read-only in shadow mode, calibrates locally, and advances only after safety review.

32
00:03:28,400 --> 00:03:32,281
Compound Zero does not replace a plant’s safety systems or its people.

33
00:03:32,231 --> 00:03:36,110
It gives them the missing context—and the time—to act before the alarm.
